BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Red Revue Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T193000
UID:red-revue-concert-2026-06-20t19-30-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/05
 /Buffalo-Charging-Drum-Summer-Solstice-Alnoor-Meralli-02-scaled-aspect-rat
 io-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Join the Aga Khan Museum and the Toronto Council Fire Native C
 ultural Centre in celebrating the Summer Solstice ahead of National Indige
 nous Peoples’ Day. The Red Revue Concert\, co-presented with the Associa
 tion for Native Development in the Performing and Visual Arts (ANDPVA)\, b
 rings together traditional and contemporary Indigenous artists to showcase
  their exceptional gifts and talents.\n\nStay after the concert for a spec
 ial afterparty from 10 pm–12 am. Enjoy music in the Atrium and delicious
  snacks from the Courtyard Café\, as well as access to the Museum’s gal
 leries.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/red-revue-concert/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Grizzlies
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T173000
UID:the-grizzlies-2026-06-21t14-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /cbc_films_the_grizzlies_ott_background_v01-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-
 scaled.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Summer Solstice and National Indigenous People’s D
 ay by joining us for a film screening of The Grizzlies .\n\nFollowing the 
 screening\, a panel discussion will explore the themes presented in the fi
 lm\, with an opportunity for audience questions and participation. Guests 
 are then invited to a live lacrosse demonstration in the Aga Khan Park led
  by Cameron Bomberry and Leon Henhawk. Note this demonstration is weather 
 dependent.\n\nInspired by an incredible true story\, The Grizzlies is a po
 werful and inspiring film about a group of youth in a small Arctic communi
 ty in Nunavut who come together through sport to overcome challenges\, bui
 ld friendships\, and find hope. When a new coach introduces lacrosse\, a t
 eam of young people discover strength\, resilience\, and the power of supp
 orting one another.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/the-grizzlies/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beyond Earth: A Conversation on Artemis\, Leadership\, and Public 
 Engagement
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T200000
UID:beyond-earth-a-conversation-on-artemis-leadership-and-public-engagemen
 t-2026-06-24t19-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/05
 /Nilufar-R-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpeg?resize=1584%2C990&gra
 vity
DESCRIPTION:Join Nilufar Ramji\, communications leader at NASA\, in conver
 sation with Bita Pourvash\, Aga Khan Museum Curator\, for an engaging fire
 side chat exploring storytelling\, science\, and the future of space explo
 ration. Drawing from her work on NASA’s major exploration initiatives\, 
 including the Artemis missions and Moon to Mars campaign\, Nilufar offers 
 insight into how complex scientific discoveries are translated into compel
 ling stories that connect with audiences around the world.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/beyond-earth-talk/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rhythms of Canada
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T220000
UID:rhythms-of-canada-2026-07-01t10-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/04
 /Rhythms-of-Canada-2024-Day-2-Alnoor-Meralli-013-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-
 1000-scaled.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Join us this Canada Day for the Aga Khan Museum’s hottest su
 mmer celebration!\n\nBring the whole family to Rhythms of Canada\, a free\
 , all-ages festival returning on Wednesday\, July 1\, 2026. Throughout the
  Aga Khan Museum\, Aga Khan Park\, and the Ismaili Centre Toronto\, you ca
 n enjoy live performances including Ahmed Moneka Jazz\, Whispr and the Lar
 nell Lewis Band\, take a kite decorating workshop\, learn Bollywood dance 
 moves or enjoy hot-off-the-grill street food. Soccer fans can cheer on the
 ir favourite team for all three Canada Day matches in our air-conditioned\
 , Game Zone Tent and catch kick-off on the big screen!\n\nAdmission to the
  Museum is FREE all day to all visitors.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/rhythms-of-canada/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Match Day Watch Parties
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260701
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260706
UID:match-day-watch-parties-2026-07-01@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /soccer-ball-museum-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.png?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Experience the excitement of soccer’s biggest summer at the 
 Aga Khan Museum. Join us for live screenings of international knockout-sta
 ge matches on a massive 20 ft x 12 ft LED screen inside our fully air-cond
 itioned Game Zone Tent.\n\nGather with fellow fans and enjoy Round of 32 a
 nd Round of 16 matches in a vibrant community setting. Whether you’re a 
 lifelong supporter or simply looking to be part of the atmosphere\, this a
 ll-ages viewing experience offers the perfect place to watch every goal\, 
 save\, and celebration.\n\nCome together to experience the excitement of g
 lobal football this summer in Toronto and cheer on the world’s top teams
  as they compete on soccer’s biggest stage.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/match-day-watch-parties/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fasayfisa’: Introduction to Mosaic Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T130000
UID:fasayfisa-introduction-to-mosaic-workshop-2026-07-01t13-00-00-04-00@ag
 akhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /Mosaic-Coster-Shirin-Divanbeigi4-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg
 ?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Discover the beauty and meaning behind Fasayfisa’ — an Ara
 bic term for small\, colourful pieces of marble or stone arranged side by 
 side to form a unified design.\n\nThrough this hands-on workshop\, partici
 pants will create a small ornament using vibrant glass tiles\, inspired by
  the intricate patterns found in Islamic art and architecture. Drawing fro
 m examples in the Aga Khan Museum Collections\, explore how these repeatin
 g designs embody harmony\, balance\, and creativity\, a tradition that has
  flourished for centuries.
LOCATION:Education Centre\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\,
  ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-roc-mosaic-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fasayfisa’: Introduction to Mosaic Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T150000
UID:fasayfisa-introduction-to-mosaic-workshop-2026-07-01t15-00-00-04-00@ag
 akhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /Mosaic-Coster-Shirin-Divanbeigi4-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg
 ?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Discover the beauty and meaning behind Fasayfisa’ — an Ara
 bic term for small\, colourful pieces of marble or stone arranged side by 
 side to form a unified design.\n\nThrough this hands-on workshop\, partici
 pants will create a small ornament using vibrant glass tiles\, inspired by
  the intricate patterns found in Islamic art and architecture. Drawing fro
 m examples in the Aga Khan Museum Collections\, explore how these repeatin
 g designs embody harmony\, balance\, and creativity\, a tradition that has
  flourished for centuries.
LOCATION:Education Centre\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\,
  ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-roc-mosaic-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Patterns in the Wind: Kite Decorating Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T130000
UID:patterns-in-the-wind-kite-decorating-workshop-2026-07-01t13-00-00-04-0
 0@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /Kite-Decorating-Workshop_Game-On_Multigenerational_Madalina-Raduta5-scale
 d-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpeg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Get creative while learning about various patterns in Islamic 
 Art.\n\nIn this hands-on workshop led by expert museum educators\, get ins
 pired by floral and geometric patterns to create your very own\, one-of-a-
 kind\, kite. After the workshop\, you are invited to try out your kite in 
 the Aga Khan Park.
LOCATION:Education Centre\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\,
  ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-roc-kite-decorating-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
